Foveated single layer (0099): without a recommended view size from the runtime, composed_size takes each side of the
composed image from the periphery's field of view at the focus layer's pixel density. A field of view that is not
finite gave a NaN span, which went through std::clamp (NaN passes it) into std::lround: a 0 wide composed swapchain
(MSVC, /O2; an infinite span gave 8192). Now a span that is not finite counts as none (the periphery image's own size, as with no focus span), and a
periphery image wider than 8192 no longer gives std::clamp a low bound above its high one. The size math moves to
xrfg::foveated_composed_side (d3d12_foveated_composer.hpp) so it can be tested; same result for finite spans.
foveated_composer_tests checks it first (12 cases): before, the NaN (0) and infinite (8192) cases fail; after, all pass.
